CURRENT KNOWN RECONCILIATION

REQ-001 overlaps existing T-190.

T-190 engineering already implements:
- vendor-specific quota/limit detection;
- delayed continuation;
- ordered subscription continuation;
- selected SAIFREN fallback;
- persisted pending continuation;
- restart idempotency;
- fresh quota recovery;
- return after refill;
- cancellation/pause semantics.

Do not rebuild those mechanisms unless regression evidence proves them broken.

T-216 remains the separate live paid-vendor field acceptance:
real subscription exhaustion and real vendor reset must not be fabricated.

The fresh bundle extends and tests the surrounding continuity system.

PRIORITY ORDER

P0 — ROUTING CONTINUITY / LOST-WORK PREVENTION

REQ-002
A dead or crashed user-local 9router must never leave an autonomous ZAICODE run
retrying a nonexistent endpoint for hours.

Build a health-aware fail-open routing supervisor.

Required behavior:

1. Detect that the configured user-local 9router process/service/API is actually
   unavailable.

2. Distinguish:
   - router process unavailable;
   - router API unhealthy;
   - temporary connection failure;
   - provider/model failure behind a healthy router;
   - subscription quota exhaustion.

   Do not collapse these into one generic inference failure.

3. For a dead/unavailable user-local 9router:
   - attempt silent recovery;
   - make up to 10 bounded restart/reconnect attempts;
   - health-check after every attempt;
   - use bounded backoff;
   - do not create overlapping restart processes;
   - do not spin an infinite retry loop.

4. If the user router is still unhealthy after the recovery budget:
   fail open to ZAICODE's usable internal fallback path.

5. Preserve:
   - project;
   - session;
   - objective;
   - scheduler ownership;
   - pending continuation state;
   - current task intent.

   Fallback must continue the same work, not create an unrelated replacement task.

6. While running on fallback:
   periodically probe the preferred local router at a sane low frequency.

7. When the local router becomes healthy again:
   return to it safely at a continuation boundary.

   Do not interrupt a healthy in-flight inference merely because the preferred
   router came back.

8. Add cooldown/hysteresis so a flapping router cannot bounce the workload
   endlessly between preferred and fallback routes.

9. Persist enough supervisor state that a ZAICODE restart does not forget:
   - router failure state;
   - retry budget;
   - fallback activation;
   - pending recovery.

10. Surface truthful status to the operator:
    preferred router unavailable / recovering / fallback active / restored.

11. A dead router must never be reported as working merely because retry timers
    are still firing.

12. Add regression coverage for:
    - router process disappears;
    - API becomes unreachable;
    - restart succeeds on an intermediate attempt;
    - all 10 attempts fail;
    - fallback succeeds;
    - ZAICODE restarts during fallback;
    - local router later recovers;
    - router flaps repeatedly;
    - fallback itself is unavailable;
    - quota exhaustion behind a healthy router is not mistaken for router death.

P1 — SESSION CONTINUITY / UI TRUTH

REQ-003
MAIN mode must not visually spawn disposable child-session rows for the same run.

For MAIN mode:
- keep one canonical project/session row;
- internal worker/run identifiers may exist internally;
- do not expose them as persistent sibling/child session clutter;
- cleanup must not depend on the operator manually deleting orphan rows;
- restart/recovery must reconnect to the canonical MAIN row;
- no duplicate MAIN sessions after scheduler handoff or model continuation.

Regression-test repeated continuation, worker replacement, app restart, failure,
and recovery.

REQ-008
Repair navigation restoration.

Scenario:
1. open project/session A;
2. open ZAICODE, Scheduler, or SAIHOME auxiliary surface;
3. select session A again.

Session A must activate immediately.

It must not require:
A -> auxiliary view -> B -> A.

Test current-session identity, route state, stale selection state and cached view
activation.

REQ-005
The sidebar control is a real toggle.

Click when hidden -> show.
Click the same control again when shown -> hide.

The action must remain correct for either sidebar side and after restart if layout
state is persisted.

REQ-012
When sidebar placement changes sides, associated controls must migrate with the
sidebar correctly.

Do not leave controls positioned according to the previous side.

Test:
- left -> right;
- right -> left;
- narrow window;
- expanded/collapsed sidebar;
- restart with persisted side.

REQ-004
Session cleanup/archive feedback must never cover the working sidebar for several
seconds.

Move transient cleanup feedback to a non-obstructive surface or make its geometry
respect the current sidebar/workspace region.

Preserve Undo.

Test both sidebar sides and narrow layouts.

P1 — AUTO RETRY STATE TRUTH

REQ-006
Treat the screenshot as a regression against T-201.

The product can display Auto retry ON while effective retry state is OFF.

There must be one authoritative effective-state calculation.

Every representation must derive from it:
- composer control;
- sidebar control;
- retry banner/message;
- session/project/global scope;
- persisted preference.

Never display:
"Auto retry on"
while the active effective state is OFF.

If global is ON but the current session/project overrides it OFF, the UI must
explain the effective state rather than showing the global state as though it
applies.

Add state-matrix tests for:
- global ON/OFF;
- project override;
- session override;
- inherited/default;
- reload;
- scope change while a retry countdown exists.

P2 — COMPOSER / ATTACHMENTS

REQ-007
Long pasted text that ZAICODE externalizes into a text attachment must remain
editable and inspectable.

Required UX:
- click/open the generated text attachment;
- inspect its actual current text;
- edit;
- save/replace before send;
- remove;
- preferably restore to composer text when reasonable.

The operator must always be able to know exactly what will be sent.

Do not silently mutate an already-sent historical attachment.

REQ-011
Move COLLECT into the compact lower composer/action row.

Do not reserve a dedicated mostly-empty row merely for COLLECT controls.

Preserve accessibility, disabled state, tooltip and current collect semantics.

Test narrow width and attachment/composer states.

P2 — WORKER LIMIT VISIBILITY

REQ-009
Expose useful 5h/weekly quota state directly on each relevant subscription worker.

The quota/window backend already has related concepts; reuse authoritative data.

Show compact visual bars/meters for the worker/account itself.

Requirements:
- 5h and weekly remain visually distinguishable;
- do not fabricate quota when vendor data is unknown;
- stale data must look stale/unknown, not healthy;
- reset information remains reachable;
- avoid excessive visual noise;
- zero quota is visually obvious.

Keep the existing global limit surfaces; this is worker-local visibility.

P2 — THEMES

REQ-010
Add a simplified non-beveled UI style.

Do not remove the existing vintage/beveled style.

Provide a small coherent family of style presets, for example:
- Classic / current beveled;
- Simple Boxes;
- Flat;
- Minimal.

The exact names may differ.

Simple mode must:
- remove decorative bevel depth;
- retain clear boxes/borders and hierarchy;
- preserve theme colors;
- preserve focus/hover/disabled states;
- remain readable at compact sizes.

Do not duplicate entire theme definitions if this can be expressed as a
presentation/style dimension.

VALIDATION

For each REQ-001..REQ-012:
- record explicit disposition;
- implementation evidence or truthful NOT_DONE/BLOCKED;
- targeted regression test where practical.

Do not accept ticket prose as implementation proof.

Run the repository's normal:
- focused tests;
- full relevant tests;
- typecheck;
- lint;
- architecture checks;
- production build/package checks where required.

For UI defects shown by screenshots, perform packaged/live UI verification when
the environment allows it.

For REQ-002 specifically, simulate router death rather than waiting for an
accidental real crash.

Do not consume paid subscription quota merely to close T-216.

ACCEPTANCE

The run is successful when:

- killing or losing user-local 9router no longer strands autonomous work;
- local-router recovery and internal fallback are deterministic and bounded;
- MAIN mode does not create visible orphan child sessions;
- navigation back to the currently selected session works directly;
- sidebar controls toggle and migrate correctly;
- cleanup feedback does not obscure the workspace;
- Auto retry UI always matches effective state;
- generated long-text attachments remain inspectable/editable before send;
- worker quota bars expose real 5h/weekly state;
- a simple non-beveled theme exists;
- COLLECT no longer wastes an entire row;
- existing T-190 scheduler continuity remains green.

NON_GOALS

- Do not fabricate T-216 live paid quota evidence.
- Do not replace SAIPEN continuation ownership with a second scheduler.
- Do not create duplicate routing supervisors.
- Do not redesign unrelated ZAICODE surfaces.
- Do not delete existing theme families.
- Do not expose implementation-only child runs as user sessions in MAIN mode.
